## 9. Error and boundary matrix

### [CXC-SUB-BOUNDARIES] Every condition a builder would otherwise have to invent an answer for

| # | Condition | Required behaviour |
|---|-----------|--------------------|
| 1 | Empty declared set | subscribe NOTHING; `*` must be explicit ([CXC-SUB-DECLARE]) |
| 2 | Mid-pattern glob (`a/*/b`) | RAISE at declaration time (`validate_pattern`, `bus.py:58-64`) |
| 3 | Declared set inexpressible in available filter units | load the narrowest expressible SUPERSET + software residue; NEVER a subset ([CXC-SUB-SUPERSET]) |
| 4 | Transport cannot enforce at all | report `enforcement: none` + WARNING naming the substrate; never a silent pass |
| 5 | Transport not taught to report | assume `enforcement: software` (pessimistic; never overstates) |
| 6 | Namespace deeper than 3 levels on a device tier | BUILD-TIME error naming the namespace; never truncate, never hash |
| 7 | Namespace with no allocation arrives on a device tier | drop LOUDLY with the namespace named; MUST NOT fall back to `namespace_hash` |
| 8 | Duplicate `(root, group, leaf)` in an allocation table | BUILD-TIME error; fail the config compile |
| 9 | Unregistered root id in a config | BUILD-TIME error naming the root and the registry location |
| 10 | `root = 0`, or an all-zero ns field on the wire | invalid; reject as an uninitialised identifier |
| 11 | Non-namespace identifier bits (type, src) in a mask | DON'T-CARE by default; pinning them narrows below the declared set |
| 12 | Child declares a namespace the host cannot subscribe upstream | explicit per-entry failure in the setup answer + host report entry |
| 13 | Slot 0 arrives at a child | log and discard; never guess, never index positionally |
| 14 | Slot with no mapping arrives at a child | discard + counter increment; SHOULD request re-negotiation |
| 15 | Child publishes `Scope.LOCAL` | reaches host and siblings; MUST NOT be relayed upstream ([CXC-SUB-SCOPE]) |
| 16 | Host publishes `Scope.LOCAL` | DOES cross to children |
| 17 | `Scope.REMOTE` across a relay | UNSPECIFIED — refuse loudly; do not choose a behaviour ([CXC-SUB-SCOPE]) |
| 18 | Payload exceeds the substrate's frame capacity | fail at CONFIGURATION time with byte counts named; the runtime path already refuses loudly (`transport_can.py`) |
| 19 | Runtime widen needing more than the boot hardware mask | coalesce over the debounce window; refuse if `filter_stability: locked` ([DD-SUB-BOOT-VS-RUNTIME]) |
| 20 | Any reconfiguration transition | pass through a WIDER intermediate state, never a narrower one |
| 21 | Peer UART, neither side on the bus | declared topology with `enforcement: none`; NOT a degraded relay |
| 22 | More than 255 declarations on one link | refuse the 256th LOUDLY pending [DD-SUB-SLOT-NEGOTIATION] |

- part-of: [SPEC:CXC-SUBFILTER]

