## 10. Acceptance — two tiers, machine and glass

### [CXC-SUB-ACCEPT] Every requirement has a machine signal; every physical claim has a bench gate

- rule: a machine signal alone certifies the logic. Anything whose truth lives in silicon or on a wire ALSO
  needs a bench observation, because a loopback test shares an encoder with itself and cannot detect a
  disagreement with real hardware — which is exactly how [BP-CAN-ID-DIVERGENCE] stayed invisible for months.

| ID | Requirement | `verify.machine` | `verify.human` (glass / bench) |
|----|-------------|------------------|-------------------------------|
| SUB-C1 | **Superset invariant** holds on every substrate ([CXC-SUB-SUPERSET]) | `tests/subscription/test_superset_invariant.py::test_enforced_superset_per_substrate` — publish declared set + control set over in-process, MQTT, CAN-loopback and a mock relay; assert EVERY declared message arrived | on the CAN bench, a declared two-entry set is transmitted and both entries are observed accepted (`STAT rxid` shows both), with `bus_error=0` |
| SUB-C2 | Superset holds DURING reconfiguration | `tests/subscription/test_superset_invariant.py::test_no_narrower_intermediate_state` — instrument the mask across a widen; assert no sampled state is narrower than the pre-existing one | — |
| SUB-C3 | Report names the ENFORCEMENT POINT per entry ([CXC-SUB-REPORT]) | `tests/subscription/test_degradation_report.py::test_report_names_enforcement_point` — assert per-entry enum + residue on the `software`/`none` entries | operator reads `_bus/subscription/report` on the glass and can state the cpu bill without opening a profiler |
| SUB-C4 | Empty declared set subscribes nothing | `tests/subscription/test_degradation_report.py::test_empty_declaration_is_deny_all` | — |
| SUB-C5 | **String prefix correlates with bit prefix** ([CXC-NSID-ALLOCATE]) | `tests/namespace/test_allocated_id.py::test_prefix_correlates_with_bit_prefix` — for every allocated namespace, `startswith(prefix + "/")` implies the id matches the prefix's code+mask; assert over the full table | — |
| SUB-C6 | Unallocated namespace refused, never hashed | `tests/namespace/test_allocated_id.py::test_unallocated_namespace_refused_loudly` — assert the log names it and `namespace_hash` is NOT called | — |
| SUB-C7 | Duplicate allocation is a build error | `tests/namespace/test_allocated_id.py::test_duplicate_allocation_is_build_error` | — |
| SUB-C8 | More than 3 levels refused at allocation | `tests/namespace/test_allocated_id.py::test_deep_namespace_refused_at_build` | — |
| SUB-C9 | Pattern lowers to the specified code+mask ([CXC-NSID-CAN-WINDOW]) | `tests/namespace/test_can_lowering.py::test_pattern_to_code_mask` — table-driven against the four rows of the lowering table | **bench**: load the derived code+mask on the C3, transmit the declared subtree plus three near-miss neighbours, observe the subtree accepted and the neighbours rejected with `bus_error=0` |
| SUB-C10 | Rejection costs no CPU | — | **bench**: 20-frame rejected burst yields `msgs_to_rx=0, rx_missed=0` with `tx ok=20, tx_failed=0` (the [CXC-SUB-MEASURED] M4 procedure, re-run against a mask derived from a DECLARATION rather than a literal) |
| SUB-C11 | Host's upstream set is the UNION ([CXC-SUB-RELAY]) | `tests/relay/test_union_subscription.py::test_host_upstream_is_union` — two children + host own set; assert the upstream subscription is exactly the union and each child receives only its own set | — |
| SUB-C12 | Child `LOCAL` is not relayed upstream; host `LOCAL` does reach children | `tests/relay/test_scope_through_relay.py::test_child_local_not_relayed_upstream` and `::test_host_local_reaches_children` | — |
| SUB-C13 | Wire carries `[slot][value]`; child parses no string ([CXC-SUB-COMPACT]) | `tests/relay/test_slot_compaction.py::test_wire_is_slot_value` — assert the framed bytes and that no namespace string crosses the link | **bench**: on `button_matrix_4x4`, an inbound `ui/led/7 = 1` lights LED 7 and the UART capture shows two bytes |
| SUB-C14 | MQTT is NOT inverted ([CXC-SUB-NO-INVERT]) | `tests/subscription/test_no_broker_inversion.py::test_socket_receives_only_declared_topics` — assert no `#`-rooted broker subscription is issued for a narrow declaration | — |
| SUB-C15 | Fat payload on a thin substrate fails at CONFIG time | `tests/subscription/test_payload_bound.py::test_oversized_binding_refused_at_config` — assert byte counts appear in the message | — |
| SUB-C16 | Unfiltered peer topology is DECLARED | `tests/subscription/test_unfiltered_declared.py::test_reports_none_not_degraded_relay` | — |

- requirement: SUB-C1 is the gate. A build that fails any other row is incomplete; a build that fails SUB-C1
  is UNSAFE and MUST NOT ship, because its failure mode is silent.
- part-of: [SPEC:CXC-SUBFILTER]

