**Status**: Draft — NOT dispatch-ready. Lowers two ratified decisions ([DEC-SUBSTRATE-AGNOSTIC-SUBSCRIPTION-FILTERING], [DEC-NAMESPACE-ID-ALLOCATED-HIERARCHICAL], both David 2026-08-10) into an implementable contract. FOUR decision points are OPEN and are the architect's to close before dispatch: [DD-SUB-SLOT-NEGOTIATION], [DD-SUB-RELAY-ROLE], [DD-SUB-BOOT-VS-RUNTIME], [DD-SUB-PUBLISH-SLOTS]. One further item is resolved-by-arithmetic rather than ratified and should be confirmed at ratify: `ROOT_BITS = 4` ([CXC-NSID-LAYOUT]) — the decision node says "4-5b root" without noting that a 5-bit root cannot accommodate `[4b group][8b leaf]`. `remote` scope across a relay remains UNSPECIFIED by design ([CXC-SUB-SCOPE]). The 29-bit identifier layout is SETTLED — [BP-CAN-ID] v2, ratified 2026-08-13, [BP-CAN-ID-DIVERGENCE] closed — and [CXC-NSID-CAN-WINDOW] was CORRECTED 2026-08-14 against it: its "the two windows coincide exactly" claim was true only of v1 and is now false, the loss of dual-filter exact matching is accepted (`DEC-ACCEPT-LOSS-OF-DUAL-FILTER-EXACT-MATCH`), and single-filter mode remains exact. Hardware claims are MEASURED on one ESP32-C3 (2026-08-10, `stamp=c8c58d8b`, Track A loopback) and their limits are stated at [CXC-SUB-MEASURED].
**Intelligence**: composed by `factlattice-editor` from the composeux-architect's narrative brief; grounded against `bus.py`, `transport.py`, `transport_mqtt.py`, `transport_can.py`, `config.py`, `transport_contract.py`, the `button_matrix_4x4` board source, and `docs/research/CAN-ACCEPTANCE-FILTER-RESULTS.md`.
